  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RJNE</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Rassemblement de la Jeunesse Nig&#xe9;rienne pour l&#x2019;Eau  (RJNE) is a member of the Global Youth Water Network, which is a grouping of young people active in favor of water. It was created during the 6th World Water Forum held in Marseille in 2012. Since then, it is present in eighty (80) countries including Niger. In Niger, the RJNE is set up in January 2023. Following the participation in theNexus Water, Peace and Security forum held in Niamey from December 27 to 28, 2022. Thus, passionate young people,concerned about the problem of water in Niger, mobilized for the creation of this network in Niger. The RJNE is a development organization whose mission is to involve Nigerien youth in sustainable development issues, particularly those related to water and sanitation.
The Gatheringis based in Niamey with a view to creating representations in all eight (8) regions of Niger.
The RJNE is an organization that works in the field of water in Niger. The animators are young graduates with various qualifications. Water and sanitation are their priorities... It is often said that water is life, and in development, water has a predominant place. The objectives of the RJNE are to - Promote the active participation of Nigerien youth in the water sector; - Promote the education of the population, especially youth, on the issue of water and sanitation; - Promote and encourage youth initiatives to solve problems related to access to water. Itsvision is to involve youth in the sustainable management of water resourcesfor a world where water is accessible to all and to all in an equitable manner. The network intervenes in the following areas - Access to drinking water; - Promotion of the WASH sector; - Rational management of water resources. Our values are: - Dialogue:we are a youth organization that works with a lot of sensitivity,several socio-professional layers, the beneficiary communities but also partners who are supposed to accompany us. Misunderstandings and/or small conflicts of competences or interests canarise from everywhere.
The amicable settlement goes through dialogue, our fundamental option. -Action: we intend to carry out works of various natures that fit with our vision of water in relation to its consumption, its maintenance, its exploitation for arational management. Our proof of existence is to act truly on the ground; - Inclusion: no one should be left out. Our actions are to be directed towards all the layers that are in need without exclusion. We need popular support with a participatory approach.
We are a newly created structure that brings together young people who are dynamic and committed to the issue of water. The RJNE is composed of very active and competent young people with diverse experiences on several themes. In terms of realization, the RJNE has just been born. It is in its first steps. It needs everyone&apos;s support. We are members of several structures with skills in several areas including water, hygiene and sanitation, climate change, agro-ecology, among others.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
